.TH RGBMATRIXFX-ENGINE 1 "2026" "RGBMatrixFX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rgbmatrixfx-engine \- RGBMatrixFX background lighting engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbmatrixfx-engine
[\fB\-\-status\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renders the selected effect at up to 30 frames per second onto Razer keyboards and mice
through OpenRazer and reacts to key presses, clicks and scrolling. It normally runs as the
systemd user service
.IR rgbmatrixfx\-engine.service :
.PP
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now rgbmatrixfx\-engine   # start now and at login
systemctl \-\-user reload rgbmatrixfx\-engine          # re-read the configuration
journalctl \-\-user \-u rgbmatrixfx\-engine             # log
.fi
.PP
When it stops it hands the lighting back to OpenRazer (or Polychromatic).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print what the running engine is doing, then exit.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/rgbmatrixfx/config.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbmatrixfx (1)
